module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TwoGeneratorPullback
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjModelStructureMap.CoefficientBaseChangeCartesian
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.PreimageOpenOfIsPullback

/-!
# The three corners of the two-generator square under a change of coefficient ring

Let `R → A` be a homomorphism of commutative rings and let `g₁, g₂ ∈ R`, with images
`f₁, f₂ ∈ A`.  The two-generator almost blowup square of [Stacks, Example 0EVH] is built
functorially out of the triple `(A, f₁, f₂)`, and the construction commutes with the change of
coefficient ring: each of the three corners over `A`

* the centre `Z = Spec (A/(f₁,f₂))`,
* the modification `X' = Proj (A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁))`,
* the exceptional line `E = Proj ((A/(f₁,f₂))[T₀,T₁]) = 𝐏¹_Z`

is the base change along `Spec A ⟶ Spec R` of the corresponding corner over `R`.  This file
proves those three identifications, each as a cartesian square whose bottom edge is
`Spec A ⟶ Spec R` and whose two vertical edges are the structure morphisms of the corners.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.centerCoeffHom`: the induced map of centres `R/(g₁,g₂) → A/(f₁,f₂)`.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationCoeffRingHom`, `…CoeffAlgHom` and `…CoeffGradedHom`: the
  coefficient extension `R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁) → A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)`, as a ring homomorphism,
  as an `R`-algebra homomorphism and as a homomorphism of graded rings.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationTensorHom` and `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.tensorModificationHom`:
  the two mutually inverse comparisons `A ⊗_R R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁) ≅ A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)`.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationCoeffProjMap`: the induced morphism of modifications
  `Proj (A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)) ⟶ Proj (R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁))`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPushout_centerCoeff` and
  `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_centerToBase_coeff`: **the centre commutes with the change of
  coefficient ring.**  `A ⊗_R R/(g₁,g₂) = A/(f₁,f₂)` because `A → A/(f₁,f₂)` is surjective and
  its kernel is generated by the images of `g₁` and `g₂`.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_modificationToBase_coeff`: **the modification commutes with the
  change of coefficient ring.**
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_coeff` and
  `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_exceptionalToBase_coeff`: **the exceptional line commutes with
  the change of coefficient ring**, over the centres and over the bases respectively.

## Implementation notes

The modification corner is `Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isPullback_map_of_baseChange`, the transport of
`Proj`'s base-change square along a graded isomorphism onto a literal tensor product; the graded
isomorphism is `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationTensorGradedHom`, built here.  Its two directions
are an `AlgHom.liftEquiv` of the coefficient extension and an `MvPolynomial.aeval` sending `Tᵢ` to
`1 ⊗ T̄ᵢ`, the relation over `A` dying in the base change because its coefficients come from `R`
(`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.relationIdeal_le_ker_aeval`).  This is the same shape as the exceptional
fibre of `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.twoGenerator_isPullback`, whose base change is along
`A → A/(f₁,f₂)` rather than along `R → A`.

The exceptional corner needs nothing new: `E = Proj ((A/(f₁,f₂))[T₀,T₁])` is projective space over
the centre, and `Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isPullback_projModelToSpec` already says that
projective space is cartesian in its coefficient ring.  Only the identification of the structure
morphism, `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.projModelToSpec_eq_exceptionalToCenter`, is proved here; the square
over the bases is the horizontal paste of that square with the centre's.

The grading of `A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)` occurs in two spellings — by additive subgroups
(`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationGrading`, the one the square carries) and by submodules
(`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationSubmoduleGrading`, the one `Proj`'s base change is stated for).
They have the same carriers, and `Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso` compares the two projective
spectra; `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.modificationCoeffProjMap` is written through that comparison, so
that the cartesian square speaks about `Proj (modificationGrading …)`, the corner of the square.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EVH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EVH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EXD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry TensorProduct HomogeneousIdeal CommRingCat
open Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlmostBlowUp

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra modificationSubmoduleGraded

variable (R A : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] (g₁ g₂ : R)

/-! ### The centre -/

/-- **The induced map of centres** `R/(g₁,g₂) → A/(f₁,f₂)`, where `f₁, f₂` are the images of
`g₁, g₂`. -/
def centerCoeffHom :
    centerRing R g₁ g₂ →+* centerRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)
    ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).comp
      (algebraMap R A)) <| by
    have hle : centerIdeal R g₁ g₂ ≤ RingHom.ker
        ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).comp
          (algebraMap R A)) := by
      rw [centerIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
      intro x hx
      simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hx
      rcases hx with rfl | rfl
      · exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr
          (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)))
      · exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr
          (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)))
    exact fun a ha => RingHom.mem_ker.mp (hle ha)

/-- The induced map of centres sends the class of `r ∈ R` to the class of its image in `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem centerCoeffHom_mk (r : R) :
    centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂) r) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
        (algebraMap R A r) := rfl

/-- A cocone on the span `A ← R → R/(g₁,g₂)` annihilates the images of `g₁` and `g₂`, hence the
whole centre ideal of `A`. -/
theorem centerIdeal_le_ker (s : PushoutCocone (ofHom (algebraMap R A))
    (ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)))) :
    centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) ≤ RingHom.ker s.inl.hom := by
  have hcond : ∀ r : R, s.inl.hom (algebraMap R A r) =
      s.inr.hom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂) r) := by
    intro r
    have h := congrArg (fun k : CommRingCat.of R ⟶ s.pt => k.hom r) s.condition
    simpa using h
  have key : ∀ g : R, g ∈ centerIdeal R g₁ g₂ → s.inl.hom (algebraMap R A g) = 0 := by
    intro g hg
    rw [hcond g, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hg, map_zero]
  rw [centerIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  intro x hx
  simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hx
  rcases hx with rfl | rfl
  · exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (key g₁ (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)))
  · exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (key g₂ (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)))

/-- The morphism out of the centre of `A` induced by a cocone on the span. -/
def centerDesc (s : PushoutCocone (ofHom (algebraMap R A))
    (ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)))) :
    CommRingCat.of (centerRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) ⟶ s.pt :=
  ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.lift (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) s.inl.hom
    (fun _ ha => RingHom.mem_ker.mp (centerIdeal_le_ker R A g₁ g₂ s ha)))

/-- The morphism out of the centre of `A` induced by a cocone sends the class of `a ∈ A` to the
image of `a` under the cocone's left leg. -/
theorem centerDesc_mk (s : PushoutCocone (ofHom (algebraMap R A))
    (ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)))) (a : A) :
    (centerDesc R A g₁ g₂ s).hom
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) a) =
      s.inl.hom a := rfl

/-- **The centre commutes with the change of coefficient ring**, at the level of rings:
`A ⊗_R R/(g₁,g₂) = A/(f₁,f₂)`.  The quotient map `A → A/(f₁,f₂)` is surjective, so a morphism out
of the pushout is determined, and its kernel is generated by the images of `g₁` and `g₂`, so a
compatible pair of morphisms gives one. -/
theorem isPushout_centerCoeff :
    IsPushout (ofHom (algebraMap R A))
      (ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)))
      (ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))))
      (ofHom (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂)) := by
  refine IsPushout.of_isColimit (PushoutCocone.IsColimit.mk
    (W := CommRingCat.of (centerRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)))
    (inl := ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))))
    (inr := ofHom (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂))
    (CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun r => (centerCoeffHom_mk R A g₁ g₂ r).symm))
    (centerDesc R A g₁ g₂)
    (fun _ => CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl))
    (fun s => CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun b => ?_))
    (fun s m h₁ _ => CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_)))
  · obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
    have h := congrArg (fun k : CommRingCat.of R ⟶ s.pt => k.hom r) s.condition
    simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom, RingHom.coe_comp,
      Function.comp_apply] at h
    simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom, RingHom.coe_comp,
      Function.comp_apply]
    rw [centerCoeffHom_mk, centerDesc_mk]
    exact h
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    have h := congrArg (fun k : CommRingCat.of A ⟶ s.pt => k.hom a) h₁
    simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom, RingHom.coe_comp,
      Function.comp_apply] at h
    rw [centerDesc_mk]
    exact h

/-- **The centre of the two-generator square commutes with the change of coefficient ring.**  The
centre over `A` is the fibre product of the centre over `R` with `Spec A` over `Spec R`. -/
theorem isPullback_centerToBase_coeff :
    IsPullback (centerToBase A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
      (Spec.map (ofHom (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂)))
      (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap R A))) (centerToBase R g₁ g₂) :=
  isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout _ _ _ _ (isPushout_centerCoeff R A g₁ g₂)

/-! ### The exceptional line -/

section Model

variable (B : Type u) [CommRing B] (h₁ h₂ : B)

/-- The degree-zero identification of the projective-space model is the coefficient map of the
exceptional line: both send a scalar to the corresponding constant polynomial. -/
theorem polyDegreeZeroHom_eq_centerRingHom :
    polyDegreeZeroHom (centerRing B h₁ h₂) 1 = ofHom (centerRingHom B h₁ h₂) :=
  CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun _ => Subtype.ext rfl)

/-- The structure morphism of the projective-space model over the centre is the canonical
morphism of the exceptional line to the centre. -/
theorem projModelToSpec_eq_exceptionalToCenter :
    projModelToSpec (centerRing B h₁ h₂) 1 = exceptionalToCenter B h₁ h₂ := by
  rw [projModelToSpec_eq, polyDegreeZeroHom_eq_centerRingHom]
  rfl

end Model

/-- **The exceptional line commutes with the change of coefficient ring, over the centres.**  It
is projective space over the centre, and projective space is cartesian in its coefficient ring. -/
theorem isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_coeff :
    IsPullback (exceptionalToCenter A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
      (projModelMap 1 (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂))
      (Spec.map (ofHom (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂))) (exceptionalToCenter R g₁ g₂) := by
  have h := isPullback_projModelToSpec (centerRing R g₁ g₂)
    (centerRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) 1 (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂)
  rwa [projModelToSpec_eq_exceptionalToCenter, projModelToSpec_eq_exceptionalToCenter] at h

/-- **The exceptional line commutes with the change of coefficient ring, over the bases.**  The
horizontal paste of the square over the centres with the square of the centres. -/
theorem isPullback_exceptionalToBase_coeff :
    IsPullback (exceptionalToCenter A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) ≫
        centerToBase A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
      (projModelMap 1 (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂))
      (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap R A)))
      (exceptionalToCenter R g₁ g₂ ≫ centerToBase R g₁ g₂) :=
  (isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_coeff R A g₁ g₂).paste_horiz
    (isPullback_centerToBase_coeff R A g₁ g₂)

/-! ### The modification: the coefficient extension -/

/-- **The coefficient extension** `R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁) → A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)`.  The relation
over `R` is carried to the relation over `A`. -/
def modificationCoeffRingHom :
    modificationRing R g₁ g₂ →+*
      modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂)
    ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).comp
      (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A))) <| by
    have hle : relationIdeal R g₁ g₂ ≤ RingHom.ker
        ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).comp
          (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A))) := by
      rw [relationIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
      intro x hx
      rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hx
      subst hx
      refine RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_
      simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, map_sub, map_mul, MvPolynomial.map_C,
        MvPolynomial.map_X]
      exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.subset_span rfl)
    exact fun a ha => RingHom.mem_ker.mp (hle ha)

/-- The coefficient extension sends the class of a polynomial over `R` to the class of the same
polynomial with its coefficients mapped to `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem modificationCoeffRingHom_mk (p : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) R) :
    modificationCoeffRingHom R A g₁ g₂ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) p) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) p) := rfl

/-- The coefficient extension as a homomorphism of `R`-algebras. -/
def modificationCoeffAlgHom :
    modificationRing R g₁ g₂ →ₐ[R]
      modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) where
  __ := modificationCoeffRingHom R A g₁ g₂
  commutes' r := by
    change modificationCoeffRingHom R A g₁ g₂
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.C r)) = _
    rw [modificationCoeffRingHom_mk, MvPolynomial.map_C]
    rfl

/-! ### The modification: the comparison with the base change -/

/-- The comparison `A ⊗_R R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁) → A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)`, the coefficient extension
extended to the base change by scalars. -/
def modificationTensorHom :
    A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂ →ₐ[A]
      modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) :=
  AlgHom.liftEquiv R A (modificationRing R g₁ g₂)
    (modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
    (modificationCoeffAlgHom R A g₁ g₂)

/-- The forward comparison sends `1 ⊗ p̄` to the class of `p` with its coefficients mapped to
`A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem modificationTensorHom_one_tmul (p : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) R) :
    modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂ (1 ⊗ₜ[R] Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) p) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) p) := by
  rw [modificationTensorHom, AlgHom.liftEquiv_tmul, one_smul]
  rfl

/-- **The relation over `A` dies in the base change**, because its coefficients come from `R`:
`f₂ ⊗ T̄₀ - f₁ ⊗ T̄₁ = 1 ⊗ (g₂T̄₀ - g₁T̄₁) = 0`. -/
theorem relationIdeal_le_ker_aeval :
    relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) ≤
      RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := A)
        (fun i : Fin 2 => (1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R]
          Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.X i)) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A →ₐ[A] A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂).toRingHom := by
  rw [relationIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  intro x hx
  rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hx
  subst hx
  refine RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_
  have key : ∀ (g : R) (i : Fin 2),
      (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := A)
        (fun i : Fin 2 => (1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R]
          Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.X i)))
        (MvPolynomial.C (algebraMap R A g) * MvPolynomial.X i) =
      1 ⊗ₜ[R] Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂)
        (MvPolynomial.C g * MvPolynomial.X i) := by
    intro g i
    have hg : algebraMap R (modificationRing R g₁ g₂) g =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.C g) := rfl
    rw [map_mul, MvPolynomial.aeval_C, MvPolynomial.aeval_X,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R A (A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂),
      Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply', Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, one_mul,
      hg, ← map_mul]
  simp only [map_sub, AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingHom.coe_coe]
  rw [key g₂ 0, key g₁ 1, ← TensorProduct.tmul_sub, ← map_sub]
  have h0 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂)
      (MvPolynomial.C g₂ * MvPolynomial.X 0 - MvPolynomial.C g₁ * MvPolynomial.X 1) = 0 :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.subset_span rfl)
  rw [h0, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]

/-- The comparison in the other direction, sending the coordinate `Tᵢ` to `1 ⊗ T̄ᵢ`. -/
def tensorModificationHom :
    modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) →ₐ[A]
      A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂ :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
    (MvPolynomial.aeval fun i : Fin 2 => (1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R]
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.X i))
    (fun _ ha => RingHom.mem_ker.mp (relationIdeal_le_ker_aeval R A g₁ g₂ ha))

/-- The backward comparison sends the class of a polynomial `p` over `A` to `p` evaluated at the
elements `1 ⊗ T̄ᵢ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tensorModificationHom_mk (p : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) :
    tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) p) =
      MvPolynomial.aeval (fun i : Fin 2 => (1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R]
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.X i)) p := rfl

/-- The backward comparison undoes the coefficient extension: a polynomial over `R`, read over
`A`, goes back to its own class tensored with the unit. -/
theorem tensorModificationHom_map (p : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) R) :
    tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
          (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) p)) =
      1 ⊗ₜ[R] Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) p := by
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C r =>
      have hr : algebraMap R (modificationRing R g₁ g₂) r =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.C r) := rfl
      rw [MvPolynomial.map_C, tensorModificationHom_mk, MvPolynomial.aeval_C,
        ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R A (A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂),
        Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply', hr]
  | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add, map_add, map_add, hp, hq, ← TensorProduct.tmul_add, ← map_add]
  | mul_X p n hp =>
      have h1 : MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) (p * MvPolynomial.X n) =
          MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) p * MvPolynomial.X n := by
        rw [map_mul, MvPolynomial.map_X]
      rw [h1, map_mul, map_mul, hp, tensorModificationHom_mk, MvPolynomial.aeval_X,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, one_mul, ← map_mul]

/-- The backward comparison sends a monomial to the tensor of its coefficient with the class of
the same monomial over `R`. -/
theorem tensorModificationHom_monomial (m : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ) (c : A) :
    tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
          (MvPolynomial.monomial m c)) =
      c ⊗ₜ[R] Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.monomial m 1) := by
  have hC : tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
        (MvPolynomial.C c)) = c ⊗ₜ[R] 1 := by
    rw [tensorModificationHom_mk, MvPolynomial.aeval_C, Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply]
    simp
  have hmon : (MvPolynomial.monomial m c : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) A) =
      MvPolynomial.C c * MvPolynomial.monomial m 1 := by
    rw [MvPolynomial.C_mul_monomial, mul_one]
  have hmap : (MvPolynomial.monomial m (1 : A)) =
      MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) (MvPolynomial.monomial m 1) := by
    rw [MvPolynomial.map_monomial]
    simp
  rw [hmon, map_mul, map_mul, hC, hmap, tensorModificationHom_map,
    Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, one_mul]

/-- The two comparisons are mutually inverse: on the base change it suffices to check this on the
elements `1 ⊗ x`. -/
theorem tensorModificationHom_modificationTensorHom (x : A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂) :
    tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂ (modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂ x) = x := by
  have key : (tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂).comp (modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂) =
      AlgHom.id A _ := by
    refine Algebra.TensorProduct.ext_ring (AlgHom.ext fun b ↦ ?_)
    obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
    simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.restrictScalars_apply,
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight_apply, AlgHom.id_apply]
    rw [modificationTensorHom_one_tmul, tensorModificationHom_map]
  exact congr($key x)

/-- The two comparisons are mutually inverse in the other order: both sides are `A`-algebra
homomorphisms out of a quotient of a polynomial ring, so it suffices to check them on the
coordinates. -/
theorem modificationTensorHom_tensorModificationHom
    (q : modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) :
    modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂ (tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂ q) = q := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective q
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a =>
      rw [tensorModificationHom_mk, MvPolynomial.aeval_C, AlgHom.commutes]
      rfl
  | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add, map_add, map_add, hp, hq]
  | mul_X p n hp =>
      have h1 : (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
          (p * MvPolynomial.X n)) =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk _ p * Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X n) := map_mul _ _ _
      rw [h1, map_mul, map_mul, hp, tensorModificationHom_mk, MvPolynomial.aeval_X,
        modificationTensorHom_one_tmul, MvPolynomial.map_X]

/-! ### The modification: the graded comparison -/

/-- The forward comparison preserves degrees: the base change is spanned by the elements `1 ⊗ x`
with `x` homogeneous, and extending the coefficients preserves the degree. -/
theorem modificationTensorHom_mem (d : ℕ) {x : A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂}
    (hx : x ∈ Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A d) :
    modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂ x ∈
      modificationSubmoduleGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) d := by
  replace hx : x ∈ (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂ d).baseChange A := hx
  rw [Submodule.baseChange_eq_span] at hx
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
      obtain ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ := hy
      obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.mp hz
      rw [show (TensorProduct.mk R A (modificationRing R g₁ g₂) 1)
          ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂)).toLinearMap p) =
            1 ⊗ₜ[R] Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) p from rfl,
        modificationTensorHom_one_tmul]
      exact Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (map_mem_homogeneousSubmodule (algebraMap R A) hp)
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ ihy ihz => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem ihy ihz
  | smul s y _ ih => rw [map_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ s ih

/-- The backward comparison preserves degrees: a homogeneous element is a sum of monomials of its
own degree, and each goes to a tensor with a homogeneous second factor. -/
theorem tensorModificationHom_mem (d : ℕ)
    {q : modificationRing A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)}
    (hq : q ∈ modificationSubmoduleGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) d) :
    tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂ q ∈
      Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A d := by
  obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.mp hq
  rw [show ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A
      (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).toLinearMap p) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) p from rfl]
  rw [MvPolynomial.as_sum p, map_sum, map_sum]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun m hm ↦ ?_
  have hdeg : m.degree = d := by
    rw [Finsupp.degree_eq_weight_one]
    exact hp (MvPolynomial.mem_support_iff.mp hm)
  rw [tensorModificationHom_monomial]
  exact Submodule.tmul_mem_baseChange_of_mem _
    (Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_monomial 1 hdeg))

/-- The coefficient extension as a homomorphism of graded rings, for the submodule spelling of
the grading. -/
def modificationCoeffGradedHom :
    modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂ →+*ᵍ
      modificationSubmoduleGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) where
  __ := modificationCoeffRingHom R A g₁ g₂
  map_mem := by
    intro d x hx
    obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.mp hx
    exact Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (map_mem_homogeneousSubmodule (algebraMap R A) hp)

/-- The forward comparison, as a homomorphism of graded rings. -/
def modificationTensorGradedHom :
    Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A →+*ᵍ
      modificationSubmoduleGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) where
  __ := (modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂).toRingHom
  map_mem := modificationTensorHom_mem R A g₁ g₂ _

/-- The backward comparison, as a homomorphism of graded rings. -/
def tensorModificationGradedHom :
    modificationSubmoduleGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) →+*ᵍ
      Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A where
  __ := (tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂).toRingHom
  map_mem := tensorModificationHom_mem R A g₁ g₂ _

/-- The backward graded comparison is a left inverse of the forward graded comparison. -/
theorem tensorModificationGradedHom_comp :
    (tensorModificationGradedHom R A g₁ g₂).comp (modificationTensorGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) =
      GradedRingHom.id _ :=
  GradedRingHom.ext (tensorModificationHom_modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂)

/-- The forward graded comparison is a left inverse of the backward graded comparison. -/
theorem modificationTensorGradedHom_comp :
    (modificationTensorGradedHom R A g₁ g₂).comp (tensorModificationGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) =
      GradedRingHom.id _ :=
  GradedRingHom.ext (modificationTensorHom_tensorModificationHom R A g₁ g₂)

/-- The coefficient extension factors as the base change along `R → A` followed by the comparison
isomorphism. -/
theorem modificationCoeffGradedHom_eq :
    modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂ = (modificationTensorGradedHom R A g₁ g₂).comp
      (Stacks.ProjBaseChange.includeRight (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A) := by
  refine GradedRingHom.ext fun b ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
  exact (modificationTensorHom_one_tmul R A g₁ g₂ p).symm

/-- The irrelevant ideal of the modification ring over `A` is contained in the ideal generated
by the image of the irrelevant ideal over `R` under the coefficient extension. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_map_modificationCoeffGradedHom :
    (modificationSubmoduleGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))₊ ≤
      (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂)₊.map (modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) := by
  rw [modificationCoeffGradedHom_eq]
  exact HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant_le_map_comp
    (Stacks.ProjBaseChange.irrelevant_le_map (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A)
    (Stacks.GradedRegrading.irrelevant_le_map_of_comp_eq_id
      (modificationTensorGradedHom_comp R A g₁ g₂))

/-- On degree-zero parts the comparison carries the structure map of the base change to the
structure map of the modification ring over `A`. -/
theorem gradedZeroRingHom_modificationTensorGradedHom_comp :
    (modificationTensorGradedHom R A g₁ g₂).gradedZeroRingHom.comp
        (algebraMap A ↥(Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading
          (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A 0)) =
      algebraMap A ↥(modificationSubmoduleGrading A
        (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) 0) := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun a ↦ Subtype.ext ?_
  show modificationTensorHom R A g₁ g₂
    (algebraMap A (A ⊗[R] modificationRing R g₁ g₂) a) = _
  rw [AlgHom.commutes]
  rfl

/-- The left edge of the base-change square is the structure morphism of the modification over
`A`, for the submodule spelling of the grading. -/
theorem modificationToBase_submodule_eq (he : _) :
    Proj.map (modificationTensorGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) he ≫
        Proj.toSpecZero (Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading
            (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A) ≫
          Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A ↥(Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading
            (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A 0))) =
      Proj.toSpecZero (modificationSubmoduleGrading A
          (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) ≫
        Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A ↥(modificationSubmoduleGrading A
          (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) 0))) := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, Proj.map_toSpecZero, Category.assoc, ← Spec.map_comp, ← ofHom_comp,
    gradedZeroRingHom_modificationTensorGradedHom_comp]

/-! ### The modification: the cartesian square -/

/-- **The morphism of modifications induced by the change of coefficient ring.**  It is written
through `Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso`, the comparison of the two spellings of the modification
grading, so that its source and target are the corners of the two-generator square. -/
def modificationCoeffProjMap :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare R g₁ g₂).modificationGraded
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).modificationGraded
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (modificationGrading A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (modificationGrading R g₁ g₂) :=
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare R g₁ g₂).modificationGraded
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).modificationGraded
  (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading A
      (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).inv ≫
    Proj.map (modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂)
      (irrelevant_le_map_modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) ≫
    (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂)).hom

/-- **The modification of the two-generator square commutes with the change of coefficient
ring.**  The modification over `A` is the fibre product of the modification over `R` with
`Spec A` over `Spec R`: the base change of `R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁)` along `R → A` is
`A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁)`, and `Proj` commutes with base change. -/
theorem isPullback_modificationToBase_coeff :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare R g₁ g₂).modificationGraded
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).modificationGraded
    IsPullback (modificationToBase A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
      (modificationCoeffProjMap R A g₁ g₂)
      (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap R A))) (modificationToBase R g₁ g₂) := by
  let := (twoGeneratorSquare R g₁ g₂).modificationGraded
  let := (twoGeneratorSquare A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).modificationGraded
  have he := Stacks.GradedRegrading.irrelevant_le_map_of_comp_eq_id
    (modificationTensorGradedHom_comp R A g₁ g₂)
  have he' := Stacks.GradedRegrading.irrelevant_le_map_of_comp_eq_id
    (tensorModificationGradedHom_comp R A g₁ g₂)
  refine (Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isPullback_map_of_baseChange
    (modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂) A
    (irrelevant_le_map_modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) he he'
    (tensorModificationGradedHom_comp R A g₁ g₂) (modificationTensorGradedHom_comp R A g₁ g₂)
    (modificationCoeffGradedHom_eq R A g₁ g₂)).flip.of_iso
      (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading A
        (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)))
      (Iso.refl _)
      (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂))
      (Iso.refl _) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rw [Iso.refl_hom, Category.comp_id, modificationToBase_submodule_eq R A g₁ g₂ he,
      projIso_hom_comp_modificationToBase]
    rfl
  · rw [modificationCoeffProjMap, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
  · rw [Iso.refl_hom, Iso.refl_hom, Category.comp_id, Category.id_comp]
  · rw [Iso.refl_hom, Category.comp_id, projIso_hom_comp_modificationToBase]
    rfl

/-! ### The exceptional line inside the modification -/

/-- **The graded square of the two reductions.**  Reducing the coefficients of
`R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁)` modulo the centre and then extending them to `A/(f₁,f₂)` is the same as
extending them to `A` first and reducing modulo the centre of `A` afterwards, because
`R/(g₁,g₂) → A/(f₁,f₂)` is induced by `R → A`.  Both composites are read out of the
additive-subgroup spelling of the modification grading over `R`, which is the corner of the
square. -/
theorem exceptionalSubmoduleGradedHom_comp_modificationCoeffGradedHom
    [GradedRing (modificationGrading R g₁ g₂)] :
    (exceptionalSubmoduleGradedHom A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).comp
        ((modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂).comp
          (Stacks.GradedRegrading.regrade (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂))) =
      (polyGradedMap (Fin 2) (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂)).comp
        (exceptionalGradedHom R g₁ g₂) := by
  have hring : (Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).comp (algebraMap R A) =
      (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)) :=
    RingHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl
  refine GradedRingHom.ext fun x ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  show MvPolynomial.map
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)))
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap R A) p) =
    MvPolynomial.map (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂)
      (MvPolynomial.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (centerIdeal R g₁ g₂)) p)
  rw [MvPolynomial.map_map, MvPolynomial.map_map, hring]

/-- **The inclusion of the exceptional line into the modification commutes with the change of
coefficient ring.** -/
theorem exceptionalToModification_comp_modificationCoeffProjMap :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare R g₁ g₂).modificationGraded
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).modificationGraded
    exceptionalToModification A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) ≫
        modificationCoeffProjMap R A g₁ g₂ =
      projModelMap 1 (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂) ≫ exceptionalToModification R g₁ g₂ := by
  let := (twoGeneratorSquare R g₁ g₂).modificationGraded
  let := (twoGeneratorSquare A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).modificationGraded
  have h1 : exceptionalToModification A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂) =
      Proj.map (exceptionalSubmoduleGradedHom A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))
          (irrelevant_le_map_exceptionalSubmoduleGradedHom A
            (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)) ≫
        (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading A
          (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).hom :=
    (projMap_comp_projIso_hom A (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂)).symm
  have h2 : modificationCoeffProjMap R A g₁ g₂ =
      (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading A
          (algebraMap R A g₁) (algebraMap R A g₂))).inv ≫
        Proj.map (modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂)
            (irrelevant_le_map_modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) ≫
          (Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso
            (coe_modificationSubmoduleGrading R g₁ g₂)).hom := rfl
  have h3 : projModelMap 1 (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂) ≫ exceptionalToModification R g₁ g₂ =
      Proj.map ((polyGradedMap (Fin 2) (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂)).comp
          (exceptionalGradedHom R g₁ g₂))
        (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant_le_map_comp (irrelevant_le_map R g₁ g₂)
          (irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin 2) (centerCoeffHom R A g₁ g₂))) :=
    (Proj.map_comp _ _ _ _).symm
  rw [h1, h2, h3, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc,
    Stacks.GradedRegrading.projIso_hom, ← Proj.map_comp, ← Proj.map_comp]
  exact Proj.map_congr
    (exceptionalSubmoduleGradedHom_comp_modificationCoeffGradedHom R A g₁ g₂) _ _

/-! ### The square over a localisation is the square over a basic open

Localising the coefficients at one element is the special case `R := A`,
`A := Localization.Away g` of everything above.  Since
`Spec (A_g) ⟶ Spec A` is an open immersion with image the basic open `D(g)`, the three
cartesian squares then read each corner of the two-generator square over `A_g` as the preimage
of `D(g)` in the corresponding corner over `A`.  The generators of the square over `A_g` are the
images `algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁` and `algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂`.
-/

section Away

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (f₁ f₂ : A) (g : A)

/-- **The image of `Spec (A_g) ⟶ Spec A` is the basic open `D(g)`.** -/
theorem opensRange_specMap_algebraMap_localizationAway :
    (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)))).opensRange =
      PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g :=
  Scheme.Hom.opensRange_localizationAway (R := .of A) g

/-- **The centre of the two-generator square over `A_g` is the preimage of `D(g)` in the centre
over `A`.** -/
noncomputable def centerAwayIsoPreimage :
    Spec (.of (centerRing (Localization.Away g)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂))) ≅
      (centerToBase A f₁ f₂ ⁻¹ᵁ
        (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)))).opensRange).toScheme :=
  isoPreimageOpensRange_of_isPullback
    (isPullback_centerToBase_coeff A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂)

/-- The identification of the centre over `A_g` with a preimage open subscheme is compatible
with the two morphisms to the centre over `A`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem centerAwayIsoPreimage_hom_ι :
    (centerAwayIsoPreimage A f₁ f₂ g).hom ≫
        (centerToBase A f₁ f₂ ⁻¹ᵁ
          (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)))).opensRange).ι =
      Spec.map (ofHom (centerCoeffHom A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂)) :=
  isoPreimageOpensRange_of_isPullback_hom_ι
    (isPullback_centerToBase_coeff A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂)

/-- **The exceptional line of the two-generator square over `A_g` is the preimage of `D(g)` in
the exceptional line over `A`.** -/
noncomputable def exceptionalAwayIsoPreimage :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (exceptionalGrading (Localization.Away g)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂)) ≅
      ((exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂ ≫ centerToBase A f₁ f₂) ⁻¹ᵁ
        (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)))).opensRange).toScheme :=
  isoPreimageOpensRange_of_isPullback
    (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_coeff A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂)

/-- The identification of the exceptional line over `A_g` with a preimage open subscheme is
compatible with the two morphisms to the exceptional line over `A`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem exceptionalAwayIsoPreimage_hom_ι :
    (exceptionalAwayIsoPreimage A f₁ f₂ g).hom ≫
        ((exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂ ≫ centerToBase A f₁ f₂) ⁻¹ᵁ
          (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)))).opensRange).ι =
      projModelMap 1 (centerCoeffHom A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂) :=
  isoPreimageOpensRange_of_isPullback_hom_ι
    (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_coeff A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂)

/-- **The modification of the two-generator square over `A_g` is the preimage of `D(g)` in the
modification over `A`.** -/
noncomputable def modificationAwayIsoPreimage :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare (Localization.Away g)
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁)
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂)).modificationGraded
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (modificationGrading (Localization.Away g)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂)) ≅
      (modificationToBase A f₁ f₂ ⁻¹ᵁ
        (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)))).opensRange).toScheme :=
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare (Localization.Away g)
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁)
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂)).modificationGraded
  isoPreimageOpensRange_of_isPullback
    (isPullback_modificationToBase_coeff A (Localization.Away g) f₁ f₂)

/-- The identification of the modification over `A_g` with a preimage open subscheme is
compatible with the two morphisms to the modification over `A`. -/
theorem modificationAwayIsoPreimage_hom_ι :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare (Localization.Away g)
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₁)
      (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g) f₂)).modificationGraded
    (modificationAwayIsoPreimage A f₁ f₂ g).hom ≫
